      "primary_message": "Stem the seedless grapes.",
      "secondary_message": "3 large bunches seedless grapes, preferably mixed colors"
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "primary_message": "Preheat oven to 225°F. Very lightly grease 2 rimmed baking sheets with oil, then scatter grapes all over. Bake, checking periodically for doneness, until grapes are nicely shriveled and semi-dried but still slightly plump, about 4 hours (see note). (The exact time will depend on your grapes, your oven, and your preferred degree of dryness.) Let cool. Use a thin metal spatula to free any grapes that are stuck to the baking sheet.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "primary_message": "The dried grapes can be refrigerated in a sealed container for about 3 weeks. (How long they keep will also depend on their degree of dryness; drier grapes will keep longer.)",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
